    "collapsible_content_6m4NDF": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_d4AFzw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes Ballistol different from standard oil products?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Ballistol contains specialized additives that enhance its capabilities far beyond basic mineral oils. While standard oil provides basic lubrication, our formula includes alkaline compounds that neutralize acids, prevent rust formation, and maintain consistent performance across temperature ranges. This makes it suitable for both industrial applications and precision work where standard oils fail.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_fJ6dxT": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does this oil perform on different materials and surfaces?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Ballistol is uniquely formulated to work effectively on metal, wood, leather, rubber, and most plastic surfaces. The white oil base penetrates deeply into materials to restore their original condition while providing long-lasting protection. Unlike many products that are limited to specific materials, our formula adapts to each surface type and can be applied at room temperature for immediate results.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_y6Qzgb": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What professional applications benefit most from using Ballistol?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Ballistol serves numerous professional applications, including precision instrument maintenance, machinery lubrication, and equipment protection. The high-quality formula works excellently as a machine oil while providing rust protection for exterior surfaces and metal parts under heavy use. Many facilities appreciate that one product can serve multiple purposes, reducing inventory needs and simplifying maintenance procedures.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_LpeYtM": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long has Ballistol been trusted by professionals?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Ballistol has been trusted by professionals for over 120 years, originally developed for the German military in 1904. This time-tested formula has proven its reliability across generations of users, from mechanics and electricians to hunters and craftsmen. The consistent quality and performance have made it a staple in toolboxes and workshops worldwide.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_JKmqAz": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How should I store and apply Ballistol for best results?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Store your bottle at room temperature away from direct sunlight to maintain optimal performance. Apply Ballistol sparingly using clean application tools - a little goes a long way. For most applications, simply apply a thin coat and allow a few minutes for penetration. The oil begins working immediately, providing both lubrication and protection that lasts longer than conventional products.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
